Subject: control mode, to play a file without the JACK transport

-C reads commands on standard input and tells where it is on standard output,
so that another program can play, pause and move in a file without using the
transport, which every client of the server shares. It starts paused.

  play        play, or go on from where it was (from the start after the end)
  pause       stop playing, the position is kept
  seek N      go to frame N of the file
  quit        leave (the end of the input is a quit too)

  ready CHANNELS FILE-RATE SERVER-RATE FRAMES     once, when the ports exist
  pos FRAME STATE                                 as it changes and twice a second
                                                  (STATE: paused, playing or ended)

A seek reuses the way a transport seek empties the ring buffer. The converter is
reset in the process thread. Playing and pausing use a short ramp, so that the
output does not click. After the end the file can be played again with a seek or
a play. -C cannot be used with -t. Without -C nothing changes.
